 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You jog past the city reservoir. The water is gone.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 79
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Millions of black balls, bobbing like a giant ball pit.",
   "from": 83,
   "to": 156
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You figure they're saving water from the sun. Smart.",
   "from": 160,
   "to": 233
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You explain it to a tourist like an expert.",
   "from": 236,
   "to": 296
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then a lab worker climbs out of a boat, holding a bottle.",
   "from": 299,
   "to": 372
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "worker",
   "text": "Evaporation is the bonus. The sun was making a chemical.",
   "from": 388,
   "to": 473
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Back in twenty oh seven, tests found bromate above the federal limit.",
   "from": 476,
   "to": 565
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Bromate is a suspected carcinogen.",
   "from": 568,
   "to": 619
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The water had bromide, plus chlorine to disinfect it.",
   "from": 623,
   "to": 697
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Add sunlight, and the two make bromate.",
   "from": 701,
   "to": 752
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "To prove it, scientists hung bottles at different depths in a reservoir.",
   "from": 756,
   "to": 850
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Bottles near the surface, in more sunlight, made more bromate.",
   "from": 854,
   "to": 943
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Cut the light by about eighty percent, and bromate stopped forming.",
   "from": 947,
   "to": 1032
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Floating covers would cost over three hundred million dollars.",
   "from": 1036,
   "to": 1121
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Plastic balls cost thirty-six cents each.",
   "from": 1124,
   "to": 1178
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They block about ninety-five percent of the sunlight.",
   "from": 1181,
   "to": 1246
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "They're black because carbon black shields the plastic from ultraviolet.",
   "from": 1250,
   "to": 1343
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In twenty fifteen, the biggest reservoir reached ninety-six million balls.",
   "from": 1347,
   "to": 1455
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Yes, they cut evaporation too. But sunlight was the real enemy.",
   "from": 1458,
   "to": 1558
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On your way back, the tourist is explaining it to someone else.",
   "from": 1561,
   "to": 1638
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "speaker": "tourist",
   "text": "It's just to stop evaporation!",
   "from": 1641,
   "to": 1697
  }
 ],
